s="new" lang="EN"><p>A hot-melt adhesive particle dispersion in which the hot-melt adhesive particles are less apt to sediment; and products of even quality obtained with the dispersion. The dispersion is one obtained by dispersing particles of a hot-melt adhesive in water, and is characterized by containing a thickener of the alkali thickening type, desirably an acrylic copolymer emulsion of the alkali thickening type or a slightly crosslinked polyacrylic acid.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne une dispersion de particules d'adhésif thermofusible dans laquelle les particules risquent moins de se déposer ainsi que des produits de qualité uniforme obtenus à partir de cette dispersion. Cette dispersion s'obtient par dispersion de particules d'adhésif thermofusible dans de l'eau. Elle se caractérise en ce qu'elle renferme un épaississant de type alcali, de préférence une émulsion de copolymère acrylique de type épaississant à base d'alcali ou un acide polyacrylique légèrement réticulé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>